Z||000009||DaRkLoRD||04-19-2000||05:09 PM||||Gold-86SE, I don't think the mention of the train/mineshaft from back to the future means this story is fiction.. I've come up with lots of ideas that later were in movies or computer games.. one I'm fairly certain that the idea was based on mine, as I was discussing it for several months in an IRC programming channel... but that doesn't mean it was definitely someone copying my idea. The game wasn't popular anyway.. it was called "UFO". I bet no one else has even heard of it. the original game I was working on with 2 friends was called "Flight", and the girl in the game was based on Dominique Moceanu, (olympic gymnast) whom I had a major crush on at the time.. anyway. Lots of people could have thought of hiding something in an abandoned mineshaft.. and as for the train pushing the delorean along a track.. I don't see how that has much relevance to this story.<BR>I can definitely see how this guy could very well have started the legend about the rocket powered car.. but his ideas about the incident inspiring parts of the 3rd back to the future movie, is just grasping at straws. I don't think that lessens from the validity of the rest of the story however.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by DaRkLoRD (edited 04-19-2000).]||||reg||1
